# A generic impl's `where` clause (Type System ch. 3): `^Loud (Box a)` needs `^Loud a`, so
# a box of items shouts through the item's impl, which lives in another module; the call
# goes through a generic function of a third module that reaches neither (`Relay.Pass`).
# Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
mod Loud
mod Boxes
mod Items
mod Relay
mod Make
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label(text=$"{Relay.Pass (Make.Boxed 3)}")
